00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.720
Leah: Agile and Scrum

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:05.970
Scrum is a framework of Agile
so the strengths and weaknesses

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:07.780
for each one is very similar.

00:00:08.309 --> 00:00:12.060
There are further ones that are specific
to Scrum, but the following ones we are

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:14.249
going to look at here are the main ones.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:16.799
Let’s first look at the Strengths

00:00:17.869 --> 00:00:19.529
Chris: Flexible and adaptable.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.650
Because the requirements do not need
to be defined at the beginning of the

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:29.500
project, changes can take place quickly
and easily in Agile and Scrum development.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.980
Leah: Creative and innovative-Team
members are more creative and

00:00:35.099 --> 00:00:38.910
innovative as there is more freedom
for change due to it being flexible

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.540
and adaptable with less rigid planning.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:46.270
Chris: Reduced time-to-market-Due
to the shorter start-up time,

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.419
frequent reviews, and the iterative
approach, Agile and Scrum developments

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:53.249
have quicker product releases.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:56.730
Leah: Higher productivity of
team and improved quality.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:02.610
Because Agile and Scrum prioritises
requirements there is less risk that

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:04.500
the project specification will increase.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.139
Higher productivity and improved
quality are also due to the team

00:01:09.139 --> 00:01:13.960
being more focused, self-managed,
responsible for own tasks, and having

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:18.070
job satisfaction due to frequent
iterations and completions of tasks.

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:24.450
Chris: Customer satisfaction-Customers
are more satisfied as they participate

00:01:24.469 --> 00:01:28.899
in the development process, their
feedback is valued, and they can see

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.740
where this is being used in the product.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:38.100
Leah: Organisation transparency-Agile
and Scrum enables other employees [who

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:43.060
could also be stakeholders] within the
organisation to be included in the project

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:45.359
which supports partnerships and trust.

00:01:46.109 --> 00:01:47.979
Chris: Now let’s look at the Weaknesses

00:01:48.209 --> 00:01:53.770
Training needed-If Agile and or
Scrum haven’t been used before then

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:56.889
there would need to be training
so all the team members are

00:01:56.900 --> 00:02:01.010
comfortable with the principles,
ceremonies, practices, and roles.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:06.830
Leah: Complexity of skills
required-Depending on the project there

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:11.910
would be a need of a mix of roles and
technical ability such as Developers,

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:14.640
Testers, Designers, and a Scrum master.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:20.860
Chris: Organisation - initial change
needs-If the organisation does not

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:24.810
support Agile or Scrum, then the
team would be working in isolation.

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:29.100
Less understanding and support would
be given from the wider organisation

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:34.130
to the team members which could
result in ‘scope-creep’ and an

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:37.870
increased workload for the Scrum
Master whose role as a ‘Servant

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:40.140
Leader’ would be to protect the team.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:45.429
Leah: Not suitable for certain types
of projects-Agile and Scrum are not

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:49.939
suitable for certain types of projects,
especially larger scale ones which

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:54.080
require a high level of certainty so
a lot of planning would be required.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.319
Chris: Agile is the opposite of Waterfall,
its more flexible, good for urgent

00:02:59.319 --> 00:03:04.890
projects, higher level of complexity, with
varying tolerance for change and bugs.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:08.370
It is often used when the team
needs to know something new,

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:10.950
such as for Apps, games, etc.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.070
Companies that have used
Agile include ‘Philips’,

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:16.820
‘VistaPrint’, ‘JP Morgan Chase’.

00:03:17.569 --> 00:03:20.980
Scrum can be used for projects
that need flexibility as it can

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:23.500
easily adapt to unexpected changes.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:28.380
It is a good framework to use for
projects that are urgent, complex need

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:32.639
quick deliverables, and a team who are
already comfortable with this framework.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:37.980
Leah: Examples of Scrum projects include
‘Saab Defense’ to develop a fighter jet

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:43.190
for mission critical software, ‘Intronis
online backup services’ for increased

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:48.635
call centre productivity, and ‘Yahoo!’
Who use scrum for over 100 Software teams.

